hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24089","Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Layth, narrated to me Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abi Ufayr al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, from Muhayyisah ibn Masud al-Ansari, that he had a slave cupper called Nafi Abu Taybah. So he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about his earnings. So he said: Do not approach it. So he repeated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Feed with it the water-carrying camel, and put it in its belly."
